A||||4||scotkb75||Emergency brake adjustment||||5||
Z||000000||scotkb75||11-17-2001||10:52 PM||||It seems to be a common problem to have an emergency brake that does not work properly.  My 84 wouldn't hold the car so I read the manual and adjusted the linkage on the cable.  The brake was better but when I checked the levers (on the calibers) to make sure they were against the stops when the brake was released, they were not.  I had to loosen the adjustment up to let the levers back against the stops, then I was back to where I started, brake does not hold car.  I have been to orge's cave and read some on the brakes but I don't fully understand them yet.  Is there some sort of automatic adjustment?  (the regular brakes work very well).  How do the emergency brakes interact with the regular brakes?<P>Thanks<BR>Scot||||reg||5
Z||000001||rogergarrison||11-18-2001||07:09 AM||||Using the hand lever all the time self adjusts them once youve adjusted the linkage nuts at the back of cradle. Making the linkage too tite will keep the pads farther out against rotor, wearing them out faster and making for a higher pedal.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||11-18-2001||07:25 AM||||I use my E brake a couple of times a week.  No problems yet.  I just developed an odd problem, though.  When I pull up on the brake lever, the teeth (don't know how to describe them--the cogs that hold the brake, at the bottom of the hand lever) don't seem to hold.  It feels/sounds loose.  If I try it a couple of times, it eventually holds.  Odd, eh?<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/patriot.gif">    <BR><B><FONT COLOR="red">Proud</FONT> <FONT COLOR="white">to be an</FONT> <FONT COLOR="blue">American</FONT>!!</B>||||reg||1
Z||000003||scotkb75||11-18-2001||10:26 PM||||All 3 of my fieros (just starting collecting them 2 months ago) have a non working e-brake.  84 coupe/auto, wouldn't ratchet, removed and found bent parts; 85 gt/4sp, right caliper locked up, pads worn down, bent parts on handle assembly, 88 coupe/5 sp, no ratcheting, haven't disassebled yet.<P>When we had our new 84 (yes, back in 84), the e-brake worked great, no problems.<P>Is there any other car that uses the calipers that are on the rear of the fiero?||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||11-19-2001||08:04 AM||||pretty sure there just chevy Citation front brakes.||||reg||1
